    "b-00-overview-decision-the-kernel-16": {
      "id": "b-00-overview-decision-the-kernel-16",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Decision.",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " The kernel's entry point is one config object, "
        },
        {
          "insert": "CreateKernelConfig",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ". "
        },
        {
          "insert": "Runtime Model",
          "attributes": {
            "reference": {
              "kind": "doc",
              "path": "10-system-design/10-runtime-model",
              "label": "Runtime Model"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " defines its fields. Injected functions exist only for genuinely app-shaped slots ("
        },
        {
          "insert": "appContext",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", "
        },
        {
          "insert": "loaders",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", "
        },
        {
          "insert": "sharedTools",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", "
        },
        {
          "insert": "createSessionBinding",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", "
        },
        {
          "insert": "logger",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": "). Every other field is data, such as catalog roots, the db handle, model aliases and prices, and tool profiles. The public surface has no adapter bundle."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-00-overview-why-adapter-bundles-17": {
      "id": "b-00-overview-why-adapter-bundles-17",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Why.",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " Adapter bundles made every host reimplement kernel plumbing and let hosts mislabel identity. Data config keeps the kernel assembling its own pipeline. New config additions must be data unless the slot is genuinely app-shaped. The bar is \"the kernel cannot know this\", not \"a function is convenient\"."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
